name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q10_2025'

question 'When rendering a list of products, a developer uses the code `<h3>{product.cost}</h3>`. Why is this considered a poor user experience (UX) choice?'

wrong 'The `.cost` property is private and should never be displayed.'
wrong 'Using `<h3>` makes the text too small for most users to read.'
right 'Without a label or currency symbol (e.g., "Price: $"), the user might not understand what the number represents.'
wrong 'The `.map()` method cannot render numbers inside of header tags.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 6

Data-driven displays must be clear. Displaying raw data values without labels (schema-UI alignment) makes the interface confusing for the user.
MARKDOWN
